    # Softmax Algorithm Design
    
    ## Overview
    Implement softmax function using Triton-Ascend backend. The softmax function
computes:
    exp(x_i) / sum(exp(x_j)) for all j
    
    ## Algorithm Approach
    1. For each row in the input tensor:
       - Find the maximum value in the row (for numerical stability)
       - Subtract max from all elements in the row
       - Compute exponential of each element
       - Compute sum of exponentials
       - Divide each exponential by the sum
    
    ## Triton Implementation Plan
    - Use shared memory for intermediate computations
    - Implement parallel reduction for sum computation
    - Handle numerical stability by subtracting max value
    - Use proper grid and block dimensions for optimal performance
    
    ## Key Considerations
    - Must avoid PyTorch operations in forward method
    - All computation must happen in @triton.jit kernels
    - Handle arbitrary tensor shapes along the last dimension
    - Optimize memory access patterns

